addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHARA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIDA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>URYU TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA CHIE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, HARUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, HIROTADA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHARA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIDA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>URYU, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, CHIE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A game system, wherein a plurality of game devices (1, 1, ...) are connected to a master game station (7) via a communication network (3) to allow communication game applications to be executed between individual game devices (1, 1, ...) via the master game station (7). In addition, the game system provides to individual game devices (1, 1, ...) personal information processing means (10, 10, ...) to enable personal information exchange between players during game application execution between individual game devices (1, 1, ...), thereby allowing players to exchange personal information in the form of calling cards with opponents via personal information processing means (10, 10, ...) at the starts or ends of games.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un système de jeu, dans lequel plusieurs dispositifs de jeu (1, 1,...) sont reliés à un poste de jeu de base (7) via un réseau de communication (3), pour permettre la transmission d'applications de jeu entre différents dispositifs de jeu (1, 1,...), via le poste de jeu de base (7). Par ailleurs, le système de jeu fournit aux différents dispositifs de jeu (1, 1,...) des moyens de traitement d'information personnelle (10, 10,...) permettant l'échange d'information personnelle entre joueurs durant l'exécution d'une application de jeu entre les différents dispositifs de jeu (1, 1,...), moyennant quoi les joueurs peuvent échanger l'information personnelle avec des adversaires sous la forme de cartes d'appel, via les moyens de traitement d'information personnelle (10, 10,...), en début ou en fin de jeu.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>